  "decisions": [
    "Only the native destruction path creates a carrier. Exhausted construction, setters, component patches and anvil renaming of raw exhausted items do not seal.",
    "26.x delegates shrink to private applyDamage without ServerLevel. A stack-local level exists only around that native call and is restored in finally; the sole sealing hook remains immediately before shrink.",
    "Fabric drops non-player owners from the lower signature. Its equipment caller refreshes only mobs; players refresh at the break hook, so there is no duplicate refresh.",
    "Vanilla elytra flight stops with one durability remaining. Tests verify real flight stops unsealed, then an explicit destructive hurtAndBreak seals the elytra.",
    "Repair entry points supply registries. Crafting matching primes private per-stack originals before native assembly. Grindstone slots receive the owning player registry provider.",
    "Native snapshots preserve exact NBT. JSON checks preserve JSON representation; JSON converts typed NBT arrays to lists. The chunked format remains read-only.",
    "The obsolete UnscopedSealingTest exercised the removed implicit-sealing API; real construction, codec and network runtime checks cover its former login concern."
  ],
  "reproduced_failures": [
